{
  "about": "Lantern Hall's painted props (guild_props.py hangs and stands them, guild_furnish.py and guild_yard.py name where; build_atlas.mjs packs them). Each is a real model with its own painted map, packed into its own tile of the atlas ([left, top, side] in pixels): a 1024 tile for a big hero piece, a 512 for most, a 256 for the small ones. Every piece made for the guild was made the Mirefen tavern's way: its front, side and back views painted with ChatGPT's image generation in the tavern stag's style (tmp/guild_props_gen, not committed), then built from them in Tripo Studio (model P2, multi-view image to 3D, Smart Mesh, quad topology, its texture from the same views); the chandelier, sconces, lanterns, candles, candelabrum, jug, barrels, crates, sacks, firewood basket, bottles, weapon rack and bearskin are pieces the project made the same way for the Mirefen tavern's painted rebuild, reused here. dense is the Tripo model as exported; bake_low.py brings it down to its triangles (welded, decimated, unwrapped afresh and its paint baked onto the new surface at its tile's side) and writes source.",
